module System/Memory

### Several readers or one writer: `viewing g` lets other readers in at the same time, `modifying g` waits until it is
### the only one. Once a writer waits, readers that come later wait behind it, so a stream of readers can't keep a
### writer out. The state is laid out as the runtime's MultiReadAccess. An agent that has to wait goes through the
### AccessManager, which stops the program when agents wait on each other (`[debug] deadlock-check`).
### :see: {AccessPolicy}, {Exclusive}, {Guarded}
record MultiRead
obeys AccessPolicy
    ### The readers holding it, or the writer bit while a writer does.
    secret state: U32
    ### The writers waiting for it or holding it.
    secret writers: U32
    ### The id of the writer holding it, or of a reader while only readers do.
    secret holder: U64
    ### How many times an agent had to wait for it.
    secret waits: U64
    ### How long agents waited for it in all, in nanoseconds.
    secret waited: U64

### Creates a free reader-writer access.
### :returns: The resulting `MultiRead` value.
routine MultiRead() -> MultiRead
    return MultiRead(state: 0, writers: 0, holder: 0, waits: 0, waited: 0)

### The AccessManager's kind for this policy: a multi-read access.
### :returns: 2.
@readonly
routine MultiRead.access_kind() -> U32
    return 2
